  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1a586b723e969462a991b263e7dd4cc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogue:
    character: {fileID: -4833260855376239280, guid: 4c74d9b45011c0a4cb33179b186c1f73, type: 3}
    character2: {fileID: -6412774339020565012, guid: ee489ea9654334b49bebfbb6cef6f549, type: 3}
    name: Tour Guide
    soundToPlay: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1cfd43b09479e4b35a0341f36b492e9b, type: 3}
    audioPitchOffset: 0
    font: {fileID: 0}
    textSpeed: 0.022
    textPunctSpeed: 0.18
    lettersUntilSFX: 3
    sentences:
    - "A lot of things had to be rebuilt after the war\u2014the museum used to be
      the Lapuz Family Manor, but it was heavily damaged."
    - Senator Lapuz decided mid-renovations to have it turned into a museum... Likely
      as a publicity stunt to turn her reputation around. And it worked, funnily
      enough.
    - "... Well, it\u2019s not funny if you really think about it, but at least I
      have a job."
    - The third was a former mayor of Sumpagita, <b><i>Mayor Fidel Lapuz</i></b>,
      who was known for travelling around the world, gathering information to bring
      back for Sumpagita!
